      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Compounds 1–3 were prepared analogously. PhSi(OMe)3 (0.94 mmol) and NaOH (0.94 mmol) were dissolved in 30 mL ethanol and heated to reflux for 1.0 h. A mixture of lanthanide salts (0.47 mmol total) and Et4NCl (0.47 mmol) in 30 mL MeCN was then added at once. The mixture was refluxed for 3 h, filtered from insoluble residue, and crystalline material was obtained by slow solvent evaporation over a few days. Single crystals were collected; products were dried in vacuum for elemental analysis and yield. For 1, loadings were PhSi(OMe)3 (0.186 g, 0.94 mmol), NaOH (0.038 g, 0.94 mmol), Eu(NO3)3·6H2O (0.16 g, 0.35 mmol), Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.05 g, 0.12 mmol), Et4NCl (0.08 g, 0.47 mmol).",
